  {"type": "split", "h2": "Repair or replace your furnace?", "image": "Gas furnace with PVC venting in a furnace room, installed by EHI", "image_src": "/assets/img/work/midea-furnace-room-pvc-venting.webp", "image_fit": "cover", "image_pos": "50% 60%", "image_credit": "EHI install", "html": "<p>If your furnace is under 10 years old and the fault is a single part, repair it. Ignitors, flame sensors, capacitors and pressure switches are routine and affordable.</p><p>If it's over 12 to 15 years old and the repair is a blower motor, control board, inducer motor or anything on the heat exchanger, run the numbers. In an Ontario winter, when a repair passes half the cost of a new 96% AFUE furnace, replacement usually wins on gas savings alone, and you start fresh on warranty.</p><p>We quote both. Compare with <a href=\"/furnace/\">furnace installation from $3,300</a> or a <a href=\"/furnace/high-efficiency/\">high-efficiency furnace</a> that cuts gas use for good.</p>"},
